{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"9fb0f07cf88c876581e85005635f598ace640e6bb65a4a164348618e24a4ccb0","slug":"simple-calcs","location":"/weather_technology/metpy_calculations/simple_calcs.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Simple Calculations","content_includes_title":false,"license":{"content":{"id":"CC-BY-4.0","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","name":"Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International","note":"All non-code content is licensed under CC-BY-4.0","free":true,"CC":true},"code":{"id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://opensource.org/licenses/Apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","note":"All code content is licensed under Apache-2.0","free":true,"osi":true}},"github":"https://github.com/kgoebber/metpy_thebook","edit_url":null,"numbering":{"title":{"enabled":false,"offset":2},"equation":{"enabled":false},"figure":{"enabled":true,"continue":true}},"keywords":["metpy","python","meteorology","weather"],"copyright":"2026","settings":{"output_stderr":"remove-warn","output_matplotlib_strings":"remove"},"source_url":"https://github.com/kgoebber/metpy_thebook/blob/main/weather_technology/metpy_calculations/simple_calcs.md","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"simple_calcs.md","url":"/build/simple_calcs-359a2df4bc9e3a01320565ec704d50de.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The simple calculations cab be done with the simple mathematical symbols\nand then add that calculation to a dataset.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"J7bO8MDF00"}],"key":"veAlqB6slD"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","value":"ds['variable_name'] = <mathematical calculation>","position":{"start":{"line":6,"column":1},"end":{"line":8,"column":1}},"key":"yIJ7lz3fZE"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":10,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"A new variable can be added to a dataset (ds) by defining the name\nwithin quote marks on the left-hand side of the equal sign in the same\nway as we did with a Pandas DataFrame earlier in the semester. Then the\nmathematical calculation can be completed on the right-hand side using\nat least one variable already in the dataset.","position":{"start":{"line":10,"column":1},"end":{"line":10,"column":1}},"key":"jsNTTLC4dH"}],"key":"fuRrNa3kY8"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":16,"column":1},"end":{"line":16,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":16,"column":1},"end":{"line":16,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":16,"column":1},"end":{"line":16,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"THICKNESS","position":{"start":{"line":16,"column":1},"end":{"line":16,"column":1}},"key":"kSREEdap8Y"}],"key":"G6GcmrhrY5"}],"key":"rpBthLMrG7"}],"key":"hKP6tSHv3m"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":18,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"To understand the function and how it works, let’s calculate the\ngeopotential thickness between 500 and 1000-hPa. Recall from previous\nmaterial:","position":{"start":{"line":18,"column":1},"end":{"line":18,"column":1}},"key":"TapmvkI66T"}],"key":"l3X5yOH9MZ"},{"type":"math","value":"\\text{1000-500-hPa Thickness} = z_{500} - z_{1000}","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"html":"<span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><semantics><mrow><mtext>1000-500-hPa Thickness</mtext><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>500</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1000</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\text{1000-500-hPa Thickness} = z_{500} - z_{1000}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">1000-500-hPa Thickness</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.04398em;\">z</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.044em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">500</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.5806em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.04398em;\">z</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.044em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1000</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>","key":"dSXVzpwXA8"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"So, to compute thickness in Python is a straightforward geopotential\nheight (z) difference between two pressure levels, the most common\nthickness is the 1000-500-hPa Geopotential Height Thickness. This\nparameter can be calculated using the following code:","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"key":"pIaZwQ9hi2"}],"key":"XPNo3MWnYE"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","value":"hght_500 = ds.Geopotential_height_isobaric.metpy.sel(time=plot_time,\n    vertical=500 * units.hPa).metpy.quantify()\n\nhght_1000 = ds.Geopotential_height_isobaric.metpy.sel(time=plot_time,\n    vertical=1000 * units.hPa).metpy.quantify()\n\nds['thickness'] = (hght_500 - hght_1000).metpy.dequantify()","position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"key":"uduNpZZM8M"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":39,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"This code would add the 1000-500-hPa thickness to the dataset and be\nable to be readily plotted. The first two lines extract the 500 and\n1000-hPa Geopotential heights from our Dataset and quantify them (make\nthem unit arrays). The third line computes the thickness from the\nvariables that we just created, then we dequantify the variable to make\nit back into a DataArray style for use in our Dataset.","position":{"start":{"line":39,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"key":"BhLgCEIeqJ"}],"key":"ua5X58bc5u"}],"key":"ukrz5Hx34q"}],"key":"IF1yPbGcfj"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"prev":{"title":"Calculations with MetPy","url":"/calc-intro","group":"Introduction to Weather Technology using MetPy"},"next":{"title":"Thickness Calculation","url":"/gridded-calculation-thickness","group":"Introduction to Weather Technology using MetPy"}}},"domain":"http://localhost:3001"}